                        



Item #:  SCP-5668

Object Class:  Keter

Special Containment Procedures:  All variations of SCP-5668 except SCP-5668-2 are to be held in separate 2 by 2 meter airtight laminated glass containers within separate 10 by 10 meter airtight containment cells. Each cell and glass container is to be kept empty of oxygen at all times unless testing is taking place in which oxygen is needed, Dr.Christine Solas is required to be in attendance for testing with the inclusion of oxygen.

Description:  SCP-5668 are small, semi-humanoid carnivorous creatures with an average standing height of 4 ft. SCP-5668 are observed to move at speeds of 20 to 30mph on all fours across any solid surface, showing the ability to run across ceilings and walls. These creatures often have deformed limbs, doubled heads or limbs, and other birth defects that seem to only help them in hunting or feeding. SCP-5668 has an unhinging jaw that can open at a 150-degree angle and close with a bite force of around 4,000 psi(17,790 newtons).

SCP-5668 have a nictitating eyelid, allowing them to keep their eyes effectively open and moist for long periods of time. SCP-5668’s skin is made up of chromatophores as well as extending and retracting papillae, it can change the color, rough shape, and texture of its entire body with intense enough accuracy that it is impossible to see it with the naked eye.

SCP-5668 has the ability to produce SCP-5668-1 when hunting or threatened. SCP-5668-1 is a singular gas molecule that duplicates rapidly when introduced to oxygen, the duplication cycle can cover large areas within seconds and usually stops duplicating once it reaches a 90 meter mostly spherical radius around the original molecule and dissipates after 30 minutes to an hour. When SCP-5668-1 is inhaled it acts as a hallucinogenic miasma that causes high levels of paranoia, blurred focus, decreased color spectrum, increased pain sensitivity, and temporary farsighted blindness due to the density and coloration of the fog. Because of the adverse effects, SCP-5668-1 is used by SCP-5668 to create a prime hunting ground.

Addendum:  One out of thirty-four subjects introduced to SCP-5668 and SCP-5668-1 at the same time have survived, remnants of the deceased subjects have led to further discoveries that the wounds in alleged animal attack cases around rural parts of Canada, Alaska, and sometimes other portions of the U.S.; are caused by other roaming SCP-5668. Other known instances of SCP-5668 have been captured and contained. Currently, ██ instances of SCP-5668 are in containment at site-89 and site-9█.

SCP-5668 has caused the deaths of █ level 3 researchers in charge of or testing on SCP-5668, video and audio logs show that SCP-5668 are not adept at outward communication but are fully capable of understanding human speech and are self-aware. Instances of SCP-5668 seem to be friendly or docile towards and answer most questions of Dr.Christine Solas, registered SCP-5668-2, it is unknown why.


Interviewed:  SCP-5668

Interviewer:  Dr.Castillo(deceased)

Foreword:  Dr.Castillo is within the inner cell standing by the glass tank containing an instance of SCP-5668.

 

Dr.Castillo:  If you can hear me, respond in some manner.

(Several loud scrapes and taps can be heard)

Dr.Castillo:  Are you capable of speaking?

SCP-5668:  (An arrange of clicking and hissing noises) Yes.

Dr.Castillo:  Are you capable of escaping your cell currently?

Dr.████:  (To Dr.Castillo) What are you doing Mark? You’re fucking up testing procedures.

SCP-5668:  Yes.

Dr.Castillo:  Why haven’t you tried to escape yet?

SCP-5668:  Not… Worth (Unintelligible) yet.

Dr.Castillo:  Why isn’t it worth it?

(Glass shattering)

 

Closing Statement:  All audio and video feed after the end point was erased, Mark Castillo's body was used for further testing and locating other instances of SCP-5668.



Interviewed:  SCP-5668 

Interviewer:  Dr.Christine Solas

Foreword:  Dr.Solas is in an airtight cell with a currently invisible instance of SCP-5668, heat imaging cameras are being monitored by Dr.██████ to locate SCP-5668 at all times.

 

Dr.Solas:  Do you have a name?

(Unintelligible clicking)

SCP-5668:  Charlie.

Dr.Solas:  Where do you come from, Charlie?

SCP-5668:  Mani- it- it- oba.

Dr.Solas:  Manitoba Canada?

(Scratching)

SCP-5668:  Yes.

Dr.Solas:  Charlie, do you have a way of communication other than English that would be easier for you?

SCP-5668:  Yes.

Dr.Solas:  Can you demonstrate?

(Pronounced clicking and hissing)

Dr.Solas:  And what does that mean Charlie?

SCP-5668:  Means… He- Hello.

 

Closing Statement:  SCP-5668 was neutralized and returned to its containment cell.








                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
